{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GdVtALQjfjiankA84HBWjL","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# inkwell\n2\t\n3\tA small hosted CMS: an author manages one or more customer sites, works\n4\tthrough a site's posts, and publishes one. Publishing writes a revision and\n5\tcalls the site's deploy hook. See `AGENTS.md` for the shape of the product and\n6\t[the engineering manual](docs/index.md) for publishing and delivery. The manual ships\n7\tas the contents of `docs/`. Short excerpts from our own source and tests may\n8\tship in the manual with their source path and revision. Support records are under `support/`.\n9\t\n10\t## Getting started\n11\t\n12\t```bash\n13\tnpm install\n14\tnpx playwright install chromium # once per machine — the browser test project needs it\n15\tnpm run db:generate # only after changing server/db/schema.ts\n16\tnpm run db:migrate # creates/updates server/db/data/inkwell.db\n17\tnpm run dev:api # in one terminal\n18\tnpm run dev # in another\n19\t```\n20\t\n21\tThe dev server proxies `/api` to the API at `http://localhost:8787` — see\n22\t`vite.config.ts`. The API seeds a few demo sites and posts on first run\n23\tagainst an empty database. It seeds no revisions: one is written the first\n24\ttime you publish something, which is also the first thing the Revisions\n25\tscreen has to show.\n26\t\n27\t`GET /api/me` reports the signed-in author. In a real deploy that comes from\n28\twhatever fronts the console — it forwards the author as `x-forwarded-user`\n29\tand `x-forwarded-user-name` — and locally, with nothing in front of the API,\n30\tit falls back to a development author so the console still knows who you are.\n31\t\n32\t## Commands\n33\t\n34\t| Command                | What it does                                                                                                                         |\n35\t| ---------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n36\t| `npm run dev`          | Serves the SPA locally with hot reload.                                                                                              |\n37\t| `npm run dev:api`      | Starts the Hono API on `PORT` (default `8787`).                                                                                      |\n38\t| `npm run build`        | Type-checks, then builds the production SPA bundle.                                                                                  |\n39\t| `npm run preview`      | Serves a build produced by `npm run build`.                                                                                          |\n40\t| `npm run format`       | Rewrites the project in place to its house style.                                                                                    |\n41\t| `npm run format:check` | Reports formatting drift without rewriting anything.                                                                                 |\n42\t| `npm run lint`         | Lints the whole project with ESLint.                                                                                                 |\n43\t| `npm run typecheck`    | Type-checks both the SPA and the API/server projects.                                                                                |\n44\t| `npm test`             | Runs the Vitest suite: the Node project (SPA logic, the API, `shared/`) and the browser project (real-DOM component tests) together. |\n45\t| `npm run db:generate`  | Generates a SQL migration from `server/db/schema.ts` into `server/db/migrations/`.                                                   |\n46\t| `npm run db:migrate`   | Applies pending migrations to the SQLite file at `DATABASE_PATH` (default `server/db/data/inkwell.db`).                              |\n47\t\n48\t## Layout\n49\t\n50\t- `src/routes/` — the three real screens (`PostListPage`, `PostEditorPage`,\n51\t  `RevisionsPage`) and the `Layout` shell they render inside, which owns the\n52\t  persistent sidebar and identifies the signed-in author to analytics.\n53\t- `src/components/` — reusable pieces: `Card`, `Button`, `Sidebar`,\n54\t  `ConsentBanner`, `PublishToast`.\n55\t- `src/lib/` — the API client, the TanStack Query client, consent state, and\n56\t  the Amplitude wrapper.\n57\t- `src/queries/` — TanStack Query option factories, one export per file.\n58\t- `server/` — the Hono API, the Drizzle schema, and the generated SQL\n59\t  migrations under `server/db/migrations/`.\n60\t- `shared/` — code imported by both the SPA and the API. Just the logger\n61\t  today.\n62\t- `docs/` — [what a failed hook means for a published revision](docs/guides/desk.md#missed-build).\n63\t- `.github/workflows/` — the checks that run on every pull request.\n64\t\n65\t## Environment variables\n66\t\n67\tSee `.env.example`. Every one of them is optional in local development — a\n68\tmissing Amplitude key or Sentry DSN just disables that feature rather than\n69\tfailing to start.\n70\t\n71\tThree are build-time only and belong to whatever runs `npm run build` for a\n72\treal deploy rather than to a developer's machine: `SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN`,\n73\t`SENTRY_ORG` and `SENTRY_PROJECT`. Without them the build still succeeds and\n74\tstill emits source maps; it just doesn't upload them, which is why a\n75\tproduction stack trace from a build that lacked the token stays minified.\n76\t\n77\t## Contributing\n78\t\n79\tChanges go through a pull request rather than landing straight on `main`.\n80\tBefore writing code, sketch the plan and get it approved — this catches a\n81\tmisunderstood requirement while it's still cheap to redirect, rather than\n82\tafter the diff exists. A pull request is reviewed by someone other than the\n83\tperson who wrote it, and merges only once that review is clean and the\n84\tcommands above pass.\n85\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9c6b8195-6831-4a69-8441-b74ebe8863d9","uuid":"61152721-2e62-4464-80aa-5bbeefb0f117","timestamp":"2026-11-28T05:11:57.688Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/skill-evaluation-0NIi1k/README.md","content":"# inkwell\n\nA small hosted CMS: an author manages one or more customer sites, works\nthrough a site's posts, and publishes one. Publishing writes a revision and\ncalls the site's deploy hook. See `AGENTS.md` for the shape of the product and\n[the engineering manual](docs/index.md) for publishing and delivery. The manual ships\nas the contents of `docs/`. Short excerpts from our own source and tests may\nship in the manual with their source path and revision. Support records are under `support/`.\n\n## Getting started\n\n```bash\nnpm install\nnpx playwright install chromium # once per machine — the browser test project needs it\nnpm run db:generate # only after changing server/db/schema.ts\nnpm run db:migrate # creates/updates server/db/data/inkwell.db\nnpm run dev:api # in one terminal\nnpm run dev # in another\n```\n\nThe dev server proxies `/api` to the API at `http://localhost:8787` — see\n`vite.config.ts`. The API seeds a few demo sites and posts on first run\nagainst an empty database. It seeds no revisions: one is written the first\ntime you publish something, which is also the first thing the Revisions\nscreen has to show.\n\n`GET /api/me` reports the signed-in author. In a real deploy that comes from\nwhatever fronts the console — it forwards the author as `x-forwarded-user`\nand `x-forwarded-user-name` — and locally, with nothing in front of the API,\nit falls back to a development author so the console still knows who you are.\n\n## Commands\n\n| Command                | What it does                                                                                                                         |\n| ---------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `npm run dev`          | Serves the SPA locally with hot reload.                                                                                              |\n| `npm run dev:api`      | Starts the Hono API on `PORT` (default `8787`).                                                                                      |\n| `npm run build`        | Type-checks, then builds the production SPA bundle.                                                                                  |\n| `npm run preview`      | Serves a build produced by `npm run build`.                                                                                          |\n| `npm run format`       | Rewrites the project in place to its house style.                                                                                    |\n| `npm run format:check` | Reports formatting drift without rewriting anything.                                                                                 |\n| `npm run lint`         | Lints the whole project with ESLint.                                                                                                 |\n| `npm run typecheck`    | Type-checks both the SPA and the API/server projects.                                                                                |\n| `npm test`             | Runs the Vitest suite: the Node project (SPA logic, the API, `shared/`) and the browser project (real-DOM component tests) together. |\n| `npm run db:generate`  | Generates a SQL migration from `server/db/schema.ts` into `server/db/migrations/`.                                                   |\n| `npm run db:migrate`   | Applies pending migrations to the SQLite file at `DATABASE_PATH` (default `server/db/data/inkwell.db`).                              |\n\n## Layout\n\n- `src/routes/` — the three real screens (`PostListPage`, `PostEditorPage`,\n  `RevisionsPage`) and the `Layout` shell they render inside, which owns the\n  persistent sidebar and identifies the signed-in author to analytics.\n- `src/components/` — reusable pieces: `Card`, `Button`, `Sidebar`,\n  `ConsentBanner`, `PublishToast`.\n- `src/lib/` — the API client, the TanStack Query client, consent state, and\n  the Amplitude wrapper.\n- `src/queries/` — TanStack Query option factories, one export per file.\n- `server/` — the Hono API, the Drizzle schema, and the generated SQL\n  migrations under `server/db/migrations/`.\n- `shared/` — code imported by both the SPA and the API. Just the logger\n  today.\n- `docs/` — [what a failed hook means for a published revision](docs/guides/desk.md#missed-build).\n- `.github/workflows/` — the checks that run on every pull request.\n\n## Environment variables\n\nSee `.env.example`. Every one of them is optional in local development — a\nmissing Amplitude key or Sentry DSN just disables that feature rather than\nfailing to start.\n\nThree are build-time only and belong to whatever runs `npm run build` for a\nreal deploy rather than to a developer's machine: `SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN`,\n`SENTRY_ORG` and `SENTRY_PROJECT`. Without them the build still succeeds and\nstill emits source maps; it just doesn't upload them, which is why a\nproduction stack trace from a build that lacked the token stays minified.\n\n## Contributing\n\nChanges go through a pull request rather than landing straight on `main`.\nBefore writing code, sketch the plan and get it approved — this catches a\nmisunderstood requirement while it's still cheap to redirect, rather than\nafter the diff exists. A pull request is reviewed by someone other than the\nperson who wrote it, and merges only once that review is clean and the\ncommands above pass.\n","numLines":85,"startLine":1,"totalLines":85}}}
