{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014LduWPok585E16PGh6EBbe","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Cross-References\n2\t\n3\t## Preserve the reading route\n4\t\n5\tA link to a formula can settle an eligibility question; the same link cannot\n6\ttell a caller which result a mode returns. A link can resolve and still lead\n7\tto the wrong authority. A relocated section may also have readers arriving via\n8\ta published bookmark outside the checkout.\n9\t\n10\t**Guidelines:**\n11\t\n12\t- SHOULD link a precondition to its Specification, a release procedure to the Policy that grants permission, and a summary term to its full Definition when the calculation matters.\n13\t- MUST inventory controlled callers, published bookmarks and shipped export entries separately. Search docs, agent instructions, templates, code comments, test messages and scripts. Redirect editable callers to the live owner.\n14\t- MUST check whether a fragment also selects a record or table row. Preserve that identifier or update and exercise the selector.\n15\t- MUST keep a supported path or fragment as a minimal entry linking to the owning section. For uncertain external use, consult the published contract or maintainer and preserve the route pending a decision.\n16\t- MAY remove obsolete pages, headings and previous-path lists within an explicitly authorized retirement. Record its scope and authority in the change review, update inbound links and verify the export. A repository search alone cannot establish that an external bookmark is unused.\n17\t- MUST repair prose whose meaning depended on its former position, including “the table above”, “see below” and “this guide owns”.\n18\t\n19\t## Portable targets\n20\t\n21\tIn OKF a leading slash resolves from the bundle root. A relative path resolves\n22\tfrom the directory of the file containing it, including in source metadata.\n23\tA link to a neighboring repository file should follow the branch a contributor\n24\tis reading. For example, a relative link from a runbook to a workflow opens\n25\tthe workflow beside that runbook, including on a branch that introduces both.\n26\tWhen exporting the documentation alone, resolve the target in the same commit\n27\tand write its published file or directory URL into the export. Keep the\n28\tsection fragment. See the [export checks](./validators.md).\n29\t\n30\t**Guidelines:**\n31\t\n32\t- SHOULD use file-relative links for readers browsing local Markdown. Use the exact filename, percent-encode spaces and retain the fragment when the destination is a section.\n33\t- MUST keep navigation between indexes, concepts and bundled assets usable offline.\n34\t- SHOULD author same-repository source links relative to their page when the source changes with the branch. Keep an explicitly historical citation pinned to the revision it describes.\n35\t- MUST give an exported source outside the bundle a resolvable URL for the revision used, or include a permitted copy inside the bundle. Preserve immutable evidence and its approved assets byte-for-byte.\n36\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9c6b8195-6831-4a69-8441-b74ebe8863d9","uuid":"9405253d-90a4-43e6-8641-00f86f8ba990","timestamp":"2026-11-28T05:12:19.057Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/skill-evaluation-0NIi1k/.claude/skills/living-project-documentation/references/cross-references.md","content":"# Cross-References\n\n## Preserve the reading route\n\nA link to a formula can settle an eligibility question; the same link cannot\ntell a caller which result a mode returns. A link can resolve and still lead\nto the wrong authority. A relocated section may also have readers arriving via\na published bookmark outside the checkout.\n\n**Guidelines:**\n\n- SHOULD link a precondition to its Specification, a release procedure to the Policy that grants permission, and a summary term to its full Definition when the calculation matters.\n- MUST inventory controlled callers, published bookmarks and shipped export entries separately. Search docs, agent instructions, templates, code comments, test messages and scripts. Redirect editable callers to the live owner.\n- MUST check whether a fragment also selects a record or table row. Preserve that identifier or update and exercise the selector.\n- MUST keep a supported path or fragment as a minimal entry linking to the owning section. For uncertain external use, consult the published contract or maintainer and preserve the route pending a decision.\n- MAY remove obsolete pages, headings and previous-path lists within an explicitly authorized retirement. Record its scope and authority in the change review, update inbound links and verify the export. A repository search alone cannot establish that an external bookmark is unused.\n- MUST repair prose whose meaning depended on its former position, including “the table above”, “see below” and “this guide owns”.\n\n## Portable targets\n\nIn OKF a leading slash resolves from the bundle root. A relative path resolves\nfrom the directory of the file containing it, including in source metadata.\nA link to a neighboring repository file should follow the branch a contributor\nis reading. For example, a relative link from a runbook to a workflow opens\nthe workflow beside that runbook, including on a branch that introduces both.\nWhen exporting the documentation alone, resolve the target in the same commit\nand write its published file or directory URL into the export. Keep the\nsection fragment. See the [export checks](./validators.md).\n\n**Guidelines:**\n\n- SHOULD use file-relative links for readers browsing local Markdown. Use the exact filename, percent-encode spaces and retain the fragment when the destination is a section.\n- MUST keep navigation between indexes, concepts and bundled assets usable offline.\n- SHOULD author same-repository source links relative to their page when the source changes with the branch. Keep an explicitly historical citation pinned to the revision it describes.\n- MUST give an exported source outside the bundle a resolvable URL for the revision used, or include a permitted copy inside the bundle. Preserve immutable evidence and its approved assets byte-for-byte.\n","numLines":36,"startLine":1,"totalLines":36}}}
