{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JSX5A6Qcyyw5V9iXGjWFZ6","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Validators\n2\t\n3\t## Check the whole documentation root\n4\t\n5\tRun `check-docs.mjs` on first adoption, during migration and after editing a\n6\tbundle. It inventories visible Markdown even if every living page is untyped.\n7\tIn a populated directory without a root index it reports the missing\n8\t`index.md` and continues checking the available pages and links.\n9\t\n10\t### Prepare the installed skill\n11\t\n12\tSet `skill_dir` to the installed skill directory. Use Node, npm and a Python 3\n13\tenvironment with PyYAML. For example, from the project root on a POSIX shell:\n14\t\n15\t```bash\n16\tskill_dir=.agents/skills/living-project-documentation\n17\tnpm ci --prefix \"$skill_dir/scripts\" --ignore-scripts\n18\tpython3 -m venv .venv-okf\n19\t. .venv-okf/bin/activate\n20\tpython3 -m pip install PyYAML==6.0.3\n21\tvalidator=\"$VIRTUAL_ENV/validate-okf-v0.3.py\"\n22\tcurl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/open-knowledge-format/open-knowledge-format/527e81aff55992be21507e97004286789126f88c/skills/okf-generate/scripts/validate.py -o \"$validator\"\n23\t```\n24\t\n25\tThe command verifies the pinned validator's SHA-256 before invoking Python.\n26\tAfter setup the check runs offline. You can also point `--validator` at the\n27\tsame file in a local [OKF v0.3 checkout](https://github.com/open-knowledge-format/open-knowledge-format/blob/527e81aff55992be21507e97004286789126f88c/skills/okf-generate/scripts/validate.py).\n28\t\n29\t### Run and interpret the check\n30\t\n31\t```bash\n32\tnode \"$skill_dir/scripts/check-docs.mjs\" --validator \"$validator\" docs\n33\t```\n34\t\n35\tThe exit status is **0** when the required checks pass, **1** for findings\n36\tthat require a fix, and **2** when a setup, invocation or execution problem\n37\tprevents a complete check. Use the diagnostics to locate each finding:\n38\t\n39\t- **Required by OKF.** A format error such as frontmatter on a nested `index.md` (`E004`) or on a `log.md` (`E006`) fails the check.\n40\t- **Required by this skill.** A living page needs a nonempty string `type`, a route from the root index and resolvable local links and fragments. OKF permits untyped Markdown and emits `W120`. The engineering check determines the type using the YAML 1.2 core schema. For example, an unquoted `type: On` is a string under that schema. The pinned Python parser can still emit `W120` for it. Quoting `\"On\"` makes both parsers read the same type.\n41\t- **Recommendations.** Upstream warnings remain visible. For example, a root index without a version declaration can receive `W125`. Check for an accompanying required finding before deciding what to fix.\n42\t- **Editorial review.** The report lists typed pages on both passing and failing runs. For each page, use its reader's question and the claim it owns to [review the declared type](./documentation-structure.md#review-the-declared-type). Root reachability and fragment resolution can pass even when a subject index omits a decision, a valid heading answers another question or a runbook sends a reader through an unrelated guide. [Trace each affected reader's route](./consulting-and-upkeep.md#verify-a-readers-route) to judge the answer and its limits.\n43\t\n44\tFor checkout links to neighboring files, add `--source-root .` from the\n45\trepository root. For immutable Markdown evidence, name each original by its\n46\texact bundle-relative path. A reachable companion can cite the source in its\n47\tbody or a local `sources[].resource` field.\n48\t\n49\t```bash\n50\tnode \"$skill_dir/scripts/check-docs.mjs\" --validator \"$validator\" --source-root . \\\n51\t  --evidence evidence/accepted.md --evidence evidence/incident.md docs\n52\t```\n53\t\n54\t**Guidelines:**\n55\t\n56\t- MUST run the whole-root check when determining whether a tree meets the required format and engineering rules.\n57\t- MUST verify each named source against its companion and original bytes. Its expected `W120` stays in the report. An additional untyped living page or a separate error on the named source still fails.\n58\t\n59\t## Focused checks\n60\t\n61\tThe individual Node commands default to `./docs` and accept another directory\n62\tas a positional argument. They retain their existing root-index and OKF\n63\tdetection for callers using them during a targeted edit.\n64\t\n65\t| Command                | Question                                                                                                                                           |\n66\t| ---------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n67\t| `check-index.mjs`      | Can a reader reach every page from the root index? An OKF route may pass through nested indexes. The legacy layout lists pages directly.           |\n68\t| `check-references.mjs` | Do local Markdown links, fragments and OKF path fields resolve? The local checker also checks rendered HTML links and images for export usability. |\n69\t| `check-glossary.mjs`   | Does each legacy flat spec have a matching glossary heading? OKF type names do not imply a glossary pairing.                                       |\n70\t\n71\t## Check the export independently\n72\t\n73\tRun the whole-root command on the exported directory outside the checkout.\n74\tLeave out `--source-root` so the check sees only the files a recipient gets.\n75\tPass the same evidence paths used for the checkout.\n76\t\n77\t**Guidelines:**\n78\t\n79\t- MUST run project gates in the checkout and the whole-root check on both source and export.\n80\t- MUST include all distributed evidence and linked assets in the export and compare their hashes with the originals.\n81\t- MUST trace an index route and a moved fragment offline, and resolve each external source against its published location or pinned revision.\n82\t- MUST report checkout and export results separately, naming the validator revision, expected warning paths and reasons, and any unresolved sources or routes.\n83\t- SHOULD exercise the example or compare the claim with its implementation when checking runtime behavior.\n84\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9c6b8195-6831-4a69-8441-b74ebe8863d9","uuid":"3087b3bb-8416-4dac-9e8a-388e61e8e098","timestamp":"2026-11-28T05:12:21.761Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/skill-evaluation-0NIi1k/.claude/skills/living-project-documentation/references/validators.md","content":"# Validators\n\n## Check the whole documentation root\n\nRun `check-docs.mjs` on first adoption, during migration and after editing a\nbundle. It inventories visible Markdown even if every living page is untyped.\nIn a populated directory without a root index it reports the missing\n`index.md` and continues checking the available pages and links.\n\n### Prepare the installed skill\n\nSet `skill_dir` to the installed skill directory. Use Node, npm and a Python 3\nenvironment with PyYAML. For example, from the project root on a POSIX shell:\n\n```bash\nskill_dir=.agents/skills/living-project-documentation\nnpm ci --prefix \"$skill_dir/scripts\" --ignore-scripts\npython3 -m venv .venv-okf\n. .venv-okf/bin/activate\npython3 -m pip install PyYAML==6.0.3\nvalidator=\"$VIRTUAL_ENV/validate-okf-v0.3.py\"\ncurl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/open-knowledge-format/open-knowledge-format/527e81aff55992be21507e97004286789126f88c/skills/okf-generate/scripts/validate.py -o \"$validator\"\n```\n\nThe command verifies the pinned validator's SHA-256 before invoking Python.\nAfter setup the check runs offline. You can also point `--validator` at the\nsame file in a local [OKF v0.3 checkout](https://github.com/open-knowledge-format/open-knowledge-format/blob/527e81aff55992be21507e97004286789126f88c/skills/okf-generate/scripts/validate.py).\n\n### Run and interpret the check\n\n```bash\nnode \"$skill_dir/scripts/check-docs.mjs\" --validator \"$validator\" docs\n```\n\nThe exit status is **0** when the required checks pass, **1** for findings\nthat require a fix, and **2** when a setup, invocation or execution problem\nprevents a complete check. Use the diagnostics to locate each finding:\n\n- **Required by OKF.** A format error such as frontmatter on a nested `index.md` (`E004`) or on a `log.md` (`E006`) fails the check.\n- **Required by this skill.** A living page needs a nonempty string `type`, a route from the root index and resolvable local links and fragments. OKF permits untyped Markdown and emits `W120`. The engineering check determines the type using the YAML 1.2 core schema. For example, an unquoted `type: On` is a string under that schema. The pinned Python parser can still emit `W120` for it. Quoting `\"On\"` makes both parsers read the same type.\n- **Recommendations.** Upstream warnings remain visible. For example, a root index without a version declaration can receive `W125`. Check for an accompanying required finding before deciding what to fix.\n- **Editorial review.** The report lists typed pages on both passing and failing runs. For each page, use its reader's question and the claim it owns to [review the declared type](./documentation-structure.md#review-the-declared-type). Root reachability and fragment resolution can pass even when a subject index omits a decision, a valid heading answers another question or a runbook sends a reader through an unrelated guide. [Trace each affected reader's route](./consulting-and-upkeep.md#verify-a-readers-route) to judge the answer and its limits.\n\nFor checkout links to neighboring files, add `--source-root .` from the\nrepository root. For immutable Markdown evidence, name each original by its\nexact bundle-relative path. A reachable companion can cite the source in its\nbody or a local `sources[].resource` field.\n\n```bash\nnode \"$skill_dir/scripts/check-docs.mjs\" --validator \"$validator\" --source-root . \\\n  --evidence evidence/accepted.md --evidence evidence/incident.md docs\n```\n\n**Guidelines:**\n\n- MUST run the whole-root check when determining whether a tree meets the required format and engineering rules.\n- MUST verify each named source against its companion and original bytes. Its expected `W120` stays in the report. An additional untyped living page or a separate error on the named source still fails.\n\n## Focused checks\n\nThe individual Node commands default to `./docs` and accept another directory\nas a positional argument. They retain their existing root-index and OKF\ndetection for callers using them during a targeted edit.\n\n| Command                | Question                                                                                                                                           |\n| ---------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `check-index.mjs`      | Can a reader reach every page from the root index? An OKF route may pass through nested indexes. The legacy layout lists pages directly.           |\n| `check-references.mjs` | Do local Markdown links, fragments and OKF path fields resolve? The local checker also checks rendered HTML links and images for export usability. |\n| `check-glossary.mjs`   | Does each legacy flat spec have a matching glossary heading? OKF type names do not imply a glossary pairing.                                       |\n\n## Check the export independently\n\nRun the whole-root command on the exported directory outside the checkout.\nLeave out `--source-root` so the check sees only the files a recipient gets.\nPass the same evidence paths used for the checkout.\n\n**Guidelines:**\n\n- MUST run project gates in the checkout and the whole-root check on both source and export.\n- MUST include all distributed evidence and linked assets in the export and compare their hashes with the originals.\n- MUST trace an index route and a moved fragment offline, and resolve each external source against its published location or pinned revision.\n- MUST report checkout and export results separately, naming the validator revision, expected warning paths and reasons, and any unresolved sources or routes.\n- SHOULD exercise the example or compare the claim with its implementation when checking runtime behavior.\n","numLines":84,"startLine":1,"totalLines":84}}}
