{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011ChUm4XtVV3xyEYSiEXjYa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0198P24UigDjNyba3tkRXEBk","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/skill-evaluation-0NIi1k/docs/publishing/publish.md","content":"---\ntype: Specification\ntitle: Publishing a post\ndescription: The three-step write a publish performs and what a caller observes when the deploy hook doesn't fire.\n---\n\n# Publishing a post\n\nPublishing a post does three things, in order:\n\n1. Write a `revisions` row — a snapshot of the post's title and body at the\n   moment of publish.\n2. Flip the post's `status` to `published`.\n3. Call the site's deploy hook.\n\nThe first two happen as one transaction: either both happen or neither does.\nThe third is best-effort — see [the deploy hook](./deploy-hook.md) for the\nretry policy and why its failure doesn't roll back the first two steps.\n\n## What a caller sees\n\nThe publish response carries `deployTriggered: boolean`. The editor tells\nthe author which case they're in rather than treating publish as either\nfully succeeded or fully failed:\n\n- `deployTriggered: true` — \"Published. The site will rebuild shortly.\"\n- `deployTriggered: false` — \"Published, but the deploy didn't fire — you\n  may need to trigger it yourself.\" See\n  [recovering a missed build](../guides/desk.md#missed-build).\n\nA draft save (a title/body edit without publishing) never writes a\nrevision; see [revisions](./revisions.md).\n\n## Undoing a publish\n\nThere's no unpublish action. A revision records what went out; it isn't an\nundo mechanism. Reverting live content means editing the post back to a\nprevious revision's text and publishing again.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":331,"cache_read_input_tokens":96258,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input