t and publishing again.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011ChUm4wUKUwt9jBdd1kefh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01L74vc5J1t8upcK4iREXqBa","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/skill-evaluation-0NIi1k/docs/publishing/revisions.md","content":"---\ntype: Specification\ntitle: Revisions\ndescription: What a publish snapshots, how the Revisions screen groups it, and the titles each part of it uses.\n---\n\n# Revisions\n\nA post becomes published together with the revision snapshot written for it\nin the same transaction. A failed deploy hook leaves both the published\npost and its revision in place — see\n[publishing a post](./publish.md).\n\n## Reading history\n\nThe Revisions screen groups snapshots by post. Each group's heading uses\nthe post's *current* title; each snapshot card uses the title that was\nsaved *at that publish*. Within a post, snapshots are newest first.\n\nA draft save updates the post without adding a snapshot: only a publish\nwrites a revision.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":637,"cache_read_input_tokens":96589,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":637},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9c6b8195-6831-4a69-8441-b74ebe8863d9","uuid":"932a6d43-9698-407f-97bc-c1d4920e6902","timestamp":"2026-11-28T05:18:21.152Z","request_id":"req_011ChUm4wLP7PtT84oDcgYif"}
