{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011ChUm5GezFQnRNXbMR5Dwa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BEbZnfKKqR8cFqLUnQSCte","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/skill-evaluation-0NIi1k/docs/publishing/deploy-hook.md","content":"---\ntype: Specification\ntitle: The deploy hook\ndescription: The retry policy for a site's deploy hook and the result a publish gets back when every attempt fails.\n---\n\n# The deploy hook\n\nBy the time the deploy hook is called, the post and its revision are\nalready committed — see [publishing a post](./publish.md). Rolling that\nback because a webhook timed out would throw away real work over a problem\nthat's usually transient and, worse, outside this app's control entirely.\nInstead, the call reports back `{ ok: boolean }`, and the publish response\npasses that along as `deployTriggered`.\n\n## Retry policy\n\nThree attempts, with a linear backoff between them. That's tuned for a\ncold serverless function taking a moment to wake up, not for a target\nthat's genuinely down: three attempts a few hundred milliseconds apart\nwon't save a publish from a deploy hook that's been deleted or\nmisconfigured.\n\nWhen every attempt fails, the failure is logged at `error` and the call\nreturns `{ ok: false }` rather than throwing, so the publish route always\ngets a definite answer either way.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":388,"cache_read_input_tokens":97226,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":388},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9c6b8195-6831-4a69-8441-b74ebe8863d9","uuid":"d2979829-f8db-4b88-82c7-297c73bf81ec","timestamp":"2026-11-28T05:18:25.671Z","requ