{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011ChUm5bv7xvHYp2imkc7YG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KEV5grKnfDjQN5MrUKULPU","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/skill-evaluation-0NIi1k/docs/guides/desk.md","content":"---\ntype: Procedure\ntitle: Missed build\ndescription: What to do when a publish's deploy hook didn't fire and the site hasn't rebuilt.\n---\n\n# Missed build\n\nThe editor shows this when a publish's `deployTriggered` comes back\n`false`: the post is published, but the deploy hook didn't go out, so the\nsite may not have rebuilt on its own. See\n[the deploy hook](../publishing/deploy-hook.md) for why a failed call\ndoesn't undo the publish.\n\nOpen the site's hosting dashboard and check its queue for this\npublication. If a build for it is queued or running, stop and follow that\nbuild. Otherwise trigger one rebuild from the host dashboard, or publish\nthe post again — publishing again also creates another revision.\n\nThe [receipt from Acme's release](../receipts/hook-17.txt) is the record\nused when support reviews that release.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":518,"cache_read_input_tokens":97614,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":518},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9c6b8195-6831-4a69-8441-b74ebe8863d9","uuid":"4013ff79-928e-4a95-9f18-1bb9b5987117","timestamp":"2026-11-28T05:18:30.164Z","request_id":"req_011ChUm5bnRKgDXbRk2eabat"}
