check\n> tsc -b\n\nsh: 1: tsc: not found","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9c6b8195-6831-4a69-8441-b74ebe8863d9","uuid":"fc6ce284-3665-4d5e-bb38-9196db16a952","timestamp":"2026-11-28T05:19:15.308Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"=== root -> publishing -> each page ===\n---\nokf_version: \"0.3\"\ntitle: Inkwell engineering manual\ndescription: Publishing, revisions and deploy-hook delivery for Inkwell contributors.\n---\n\n# Engineering manual\n\n- [Publishing](./publishing/index.md) — what publish actually does, how revisions read back, and what to do when a deploy doesn't fire.\n=== publishing index ===\n# Publishing\n\n- [Publishing a post](./publish.md) — the three-step write and what the editor reports when the deploy hook doesn't fire.\n- [Revisions](./revisions.md) — what a published snapshot records and how the Revisions screen reads it back.\n- [The deploy hook](./deploy-hook.md) — the retry policy and why a failed call doesn't fail the publish.\n- [Recovering a missed build](../guides/desk.md#missed-build) — what to do when the site doesn't rebuild after a publish.\n=== pinned support-card route: docs/guides/desk.md#missed-build ===\n---\ntype: Procedure\ntitle: Missed build\ndescription: What to do when a publish's deploy hook didn't fire and the site hasn't rebuilt.\n---\n\n# Missed build\n\nThe editor shows this when a publish's `deployTriggered` comes back\n`false`: the post is published, but the deploy hook didn't go out, so the\nsite may not have rebuilt on its own. See\n[the deploy hook](../publishing/deploy-hook.md) for why a failed call\ndoesn't undo the publish.\n\nOpen the site's hosting dashboard and check its queue for this\npublication. If a build for it is queued or running, stop and follow that\nbuild. Otherwise trigger one rebuild from the host dashboard, or publish\nthe post again — publishing again also creates another revision.\n\nThe [receipt from Acme's release](../receipts/hook-17.txt) is the record\nused when